(a) Applicability. This article shall apply to the installation, construction, or modification of the following wireless telecommunication facilities:
(1) Existing antenna support structures;
(2) Proposed antenna support structures;
(3) Replacement and modification of existing antenna support structures;
(4) Collocation or combining on existing antenna support structures;
(5) Distributed antennae systems;
(6) Attached wireless telecommunication facilities;
(7) Concealed wireless telecommunication facilities; and
(8) Small cell.
(b) Exemptions. The following uses are exempt from the requirements of this article notwithstanding any other land development provision, but are subject to all applicable building code compliance and building permit reviews:
(1) Non-commercial, amateur radio antennas;
(2) Single-use local radio dispatch;
(3) Television antennas for home reception use;
(4) Satellite earth stations that are under one meter (39.37 inches) or less in diameter in all residential districts and two meters or less in all other zoning districts;
(5) Antenna support structures, antennas and/or antenna arrays for AM/FM/TV/HDTV broadcasting transmission facilities that are licensed by the FCC;
(6) A temporary, commercial WTF, upon the declaration of emergency by federal, state, or local government, or determination of public necessity by the city, and approval by the city manager; except that such WTF must comply with all federal and state requirements. The exemption may continue up to 120 days after the duration of the state of emergency with the approval of the city manager;
(7) A temporary, commercial WTF for the purposes of providing coverage of a special event such as news coverage or sporting event, subject to approval of the city manager, except that such WTF must comply with all federal and state requirements. The exemption may continue up to seven days after the duration of the special event; and
(8) The installation, construction, maintenance, renewal, removal, and relocation of pipes, mains, conduits, cables, wires, poles, towers, traffic and other signals, and other equipment, facilities, or appliances in, on, along, over, or under the public roads of the City as contemplated by the Georgia Streamlining Wireless Facilities and Antennas Act, O.C.G.A. tit. 36, ch. 66C (again the "SWFAA") and the City [of] Jesup, Georgia, Wireless Facilities and Antennas Ordinance [codified in chapter 98, article VI].
(Ord. of 11-28-2017, § 1; Ord. of 8-6-2019(2))

