1313:
(a) The city tree board shall be composed of seven members. Each commissioner from each commission district will appoint one member, totaling six members, and the mayor will appoint one additional member, to comprise the seven-member board. The appointed members shall be registered voters of the city. No member of the tree board shall be persons who hold elected public office in the city or Wayne County, Georgia. Appointments to the tree board shall be for overlapping terms of three years with terms expiring on December 31. With the exception of those appointments addressed in subsection (b) of this section, the regular initial appointments to the tree board which first occur after the passage of this section (which such initial appointments shall occur after the expiration of the current terms of the members of the tree board expire) shall be made so that the terms of said members shall be staggered. In order to establish staggered terms, the initial terms of two members shall be one year, and the initial terms of another two members will be two years, and the initial terms of another three members will be for three years. The members serving the one-year terms, the two-year terms, and the three-year terms shall be determined by agreement of the board of commissioners of the city and mayor or by lot in the absence of such agreement. If at the end of any term of office of a member, a successor thereto shall not have been appointed, then the member whose term of office shall have expired shall continue to hold office until his or her successor shall be so appointed. Any vacancy in the tree board shall be filled by appointment by the commissioner or mayor who made the original appointment to the tree board that is then vacant. In the event of the absence or vacancy of the commissioner or mayor who made such original appointment to the tree board, any such vacancy in the tree board shall be appointed by an affirmative majority vote of the remaining commissioners and the mayor. Members of the tree board can serve successive terms without limit. The members of the tree board shall receive no compensation for their services, and shall at all times maintain a current mailing address and telephone number on file with the city.
(b) Following the passage of this section, the board of commissioners will make any additional appointments to such board necessitated by the increase in the number of the members of such board under this section by a majority vote of the commissioners and mayor.
(c) The board of commissioners of the city shall be authorized to remove any member for cause after written notice and public hearing. Any one or more of the following shall constitute a reason for removing a member "for cause":
(1) Participating as a member of the tree board at any regular or called meeting of the tree board under the influence of intoxicants, alcohol, or unprescribed or illegal drugs or using, possessing or selling the same in violation of the laws of the State of Georgia;
(2) Charge and accusation for a misdemeanor which would adversely affect performance of his or her duties as a member of the tree board;
(3) Conduct unbecoming of a member of the tree board, including, but not limited to, demeaning conduct or use of profanity or vulgar language during any open public meeting of the tree board;
(4) Indictment of a felony;
(5) Unauthorized use of city property, city telephones or other city communication equipment;
(6) Filing false expense reports;
(7) Three consecutive absences from tree board meetings without obtaining prior approval of a majority of the remaining members of the tree board; or
(8) Repeated and continued discourteous treatment of members of the public during tree board meetings after being admonished concerning such conduct by the board of commissioners of the city.
Charges for "removable for cause" may be made by any city commissioner, any member of the tree board or by any citizen of the city. Any such charges must be made in writing, dated, signed and delivered to the board of commissioners of the city. A copy of any such charge must be mailed to the person making the charge to the member of the tree board against whom the charge is directed. Upon receipt of any such charge the board of commissioners of the city will then set a date and time for a public hearing. The city manager will notify both the party making the charge and the member of the tree board against whom the charges are directed of the date, time and place of the public hearing. The member of the tree board against whom charges are made shall have at least two weeks notice prior to the date set for the public hearing to prepare for the public hearing. In the event, after the public hearing, the board of commissioners of the city, by majority vote, removes the member of the tree board, the board of commissioners of the city will then proceed to fill the vacancy for the unexpired term pursuant to the foregoing provisions of this section.
(d) Ex officio members shall be: (1) one member of the board of commissioners of the city as selected by the mayor, (2) the city employee responsible for planting, maintenance and removal of trees, shrubs and vines on city property (presently the superintendent of streets and sanitation or his or her representative), and (3) the Wayne County, Georgia Forester.
(e) During the first month after being appointed after the passage of this section, and at the first meeting after July 1 of each year, the tree board shall elect: (1) a chairman, (2) a vice-chairman and (3) a secretary-treasurer from among its appointed members.
(f) The tree board shall meet at least once during each quarter of the year during January, April, July and October. Additional meetings may be held as requested by the chairman. A quorum shall consist of three appointed members. If the chairman or vice-chairman is not present, the members present, by majority vote, shall designate one of the members to serve as acting chairman for that meeting.
(g) During June of each year, the tree board shall submit a report on its activities during the past year to the board of commissioners of the city.
(Code 1976, § 2-135; Ord. No. 2017-006, § 1, 2-7-2017)
